  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The first day of spring 2026 in the USA (Northern Hemisphere) is Friday, March 20, 2026. The astronomical spring, or vernal equinox, occurs at 10:46 a.m. ET (8:46 a.m. MT). This day marks equal daylight and darkness, signaling the start of the spring season, which lasts until the summer solstice on June 21. When: Friday, March 20, 2026. Time: 10:46 a.m. Eastern Time / 9:46 a.m. Central Time / 8:46 a.m. Mountain Time. Significance: It is the vernal equinox, when the sun passes directly over the Earth's equator. Weather Impact: While meteorological spring began on March 1, this astronomical start marks the official beginning of the season.",
